18. PHILOSOPHY
EWSW-2.0 is inspired by the philosophy of Eclipses Wonder of Software and Work.
Its principles are expressions of the Creator's beliefs and motivations, not mandatory rules governing Recipients.
Recipients are free to disagree with EWSW, reject its philosophy, make money from the Work, withhold their modifications, discontinue their projects, or use the Work for purposes the Creator would not personally support, subject to applicable law and rights outside the scope of this license.
The Creator's rejection of reward does not prohibit voluntary rewards.
The Creator's preference for free and voluntary work does not require anyone else to work for free.
The Creator's commitment to people over profits does not prohibit recipients from earning profits.
The Creator's willingness to give does not create an obligation for anyone else to give.
The philosophy belongs to the Creator.
The freedoms belong to the Recipient.
19. INTERPRETATION AND SEVERABILITY
19.1. Freedom-Favoring Interpretation.
EWSW-2.0 shall be interpreted in favor of the greatest practical freedom for Recipients that applicable law permits.
19.2. Severability.
If a provision is determined to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall remain effective to the maximum extent permitted by law.
19.3. Limited Invalidity.
Any invalid or unenforceable provision shall be limited or interpreted only to the extent necessary to address the legal defect, where applicable law permits such an approach.
19.4. No Implied Obligations.
No obligation to pay, attribute, contribute, publish modifications, maintain the Work, or provide support shall be implied merely from receiving or using the Work.
